CloudBurrow patch 19 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1373). Applies after patch 0018.

tables.insert made a table's RECORD fields in the engine with their
names unquoted (STRUCT<in ner INT64>), so a RECORD whose field has a
flexible column name, which BigQuery allows (a Parquet load under
columnNameCharacterMap V2 makes one: "in ner!" becomes "in ner_"), or is
a keyword, failed "Syntax error: Expected ">" but got keyword IN". The
field's name is now quoted, as a top-level column's is.

